//? Title: Segmentation overlap, sorted IoU and boundary losses
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Learning a foreground mask needs an objective that handles overlap, missed pixels and boundary geometry. Hand-checkable values and derivatives introduce Dice,Tversky,Lovász and boundary terms, followed by exact tensor distance maps and four explicit Adam fits to one known mask.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/segmentation_losses.cpp`.

> The method

Dice and Tversky compare soft region overlap; Lovász weights sorted class errors by changes in Jaccard loss; a detached signed-distance map adds boundary geometry. All numerical computation uses tensors, including masks, sorting, Jaccard increments, distance transforms and optimization.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/segmentation_losses_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/segmentation_losses_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/segmentation_losses_concept.tikz > build/segmentation_losses_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/segmentation_losses_concept.svg build/segmentation_losses_concept.dvi > build/segmentation_losses_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
