> A four-pixel overlap and derivative calculation

Let foreground probabilities be `[.8,.3,.4,.1]` and truth `[1,0,1,0]`.
Then TP=1.2, FP=.4 and FN=.8. Tversky loss is
`1-(TP+epsilon)/(TP+alpha*FP+beta*FN+epsilon)`, with epsilon1e-6.
Dice chooses alpha=beta=.5, giving denominator1.8+epsilon. The default
Tversky alpha=.3/beta=.7 gives1.88+epsilon and penalizes missed foreground more.
Class losses pool pixels across the batch before averaging selected classes;
`first_class=1` omits background. Out-of-range integer labels are void.

Lovász sorts absolute class errors `[.6,.3,.2,.1]` with stable lower-index ties.
The sorted Jaccard increments are `[1/2,1/6,1/3,0]`, so the loss is5/12.
Sorting is detached and uses Float32 errors to preserve the source convention;
values and gradients retain the input dtype. Absent classes are skipped only
for Lovász; Dice/Tversky retain their selected-class average. All-void inputs
produce zero value and zero probability derivatives.

Boundary loss is `mean(probability*signed_distance)`. For distances
`[-2,0,1,3]`, it equals-.225 and its four derivatives are `[-.5,0,.25,.75]`.
A negative value is expected. Distances are detached and the boundary term
supplements a region loss.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/segmentation_losses_fixture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto type = n::DType::Float64;
  const auto y = n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{1, 0, 1, 0}, {1, 1, 4}),
             distance = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{-2, 0, 1, 3}, {1, 1, 4, 1});
  const std::array<std::string, 4> names = {"Dice", "Tversky", "Lovasz", "boundary"};
  const std::array<dm::graphics::RGB, 4> colors = {
      {{37, 99, 235}, {22, 163, 74}, {147, 51, 234}, {220, 38, 38}}};
  auto values = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), derivatives = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  double error = 0;
  const double expected[] = {1. - (1.2 + 1e-6) / (1.8 + 1e-6),
                             1. - (1.2 + 1e-6) / (1.88 + 1e-6), 5. / 12, -.225};
  std::print("| loss | value | foreground derivatives |\n|---|---:|---|\n");
  for (int which = 0; which < 4; ++which) {
    auto p = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{.2, .8, .7, .3, .6, .4, .9, .1}, {1, 1, 4, 2})
                 .requires_grad_();
    const auto loss = which == 0   ? m::SoftDiceLoss(p, y, 2)
                      : which == 1 ? m::SoftTverskyLoss(p, y, 2)
                      : which == 2 ? m::LovaszSoftmaxLoss(p, y, 2, 1)
                                   : m::BoundaryLoss(n::slice_axis(p, 3, 1, 2), distance);
    const auto g = n::slice_axis(n::grad(loss, {p})[0], 3, 1, 2).reshape({4});
    error = std::max(error, std::abs(loss.item() - expected[which]));
    values.bars({double(which + 1)}, {loss.item()}, names[which], colors[which], .6);
    derivatives.lines({1, 2, 3, 4}, g.to_vector<double>(), names[which], colors[which]);
    std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.6f}, {:.6f}, {:.6f}, {:.6f} |\n", names[which], loss.item(),
               g.at({0}), g.at({1}), g.at({2}), g.at({3}));
  }
  if (error > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  values.title("Four-pixel loss values")
      .x_label("1 Dice;2 Tversky;3 Lovasz;4 boundary")
      .y_label("loss")
      .x_limits(.4, 4.7)
      .y_limits(-.32, .7);
  derivatives.title("Foreground probability derivatives")
      .x_label("pixel index1 to4")
      .y_label("derivative")
      .y_limits(-.7, 1.2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(values)
      .add(derivatives)
      .size(1200, 530)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/segmentation_losses_fixture.svg");
  std::print("Independent scalar values agree to {:.12f}; native tests check every "
             "quotient-rule and sorted subgradient, perfect/absent/void cases.\n",
             error);
}
```
