> Exact tensor distance maps and the discrete boundary convention

For each foreground class, outside pixels have positive Euclidean distance to
foreground. Inside pixels use `-(distance_to_background-1)`, making boundary
foreground pixels zero. Empty/full foreground classes have zero maps because
they have no internal boundary. Void pixels participate as background in the
distance topology but receive zero map values.

The original example used a linear-time host lower-envelope transform. This
conversion performs exact separable tensor minima instead: horizontal squared
distances followed by vertical squared distances. Work is
O(H*W*(H+W)), with O(H*W*max(H,W)) temporary storage. The maps agree with the
same nearest-seed definition; this is a transparent implementation tradeoff,
not a linear-time performance claim. Native checks compare every value on100
random rectangular grids with exhaustive nearest-seed search, including no seeds.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/segmentation_losses_distance.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto y = n::arange(0, 5).reshape({5, 1}), x = n::arange(0, 7).reshape({1, 7});
  const auto mask = n::logical_and(n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(y, 1.), n::less(y, 4.)),
                                   n::logical_and(n::greater_equal(x, 2.), n::less(x, 5.)));
  const auto labels = mask.to(n::DType::Int64).reshape({1, 5, 7}),
             distance = m::SignedBoundaryDistances(labels, 2).reshape({5, 7});
  if (distance.at({2, 3}) != -1 || distance.at({1, 2}) != 0 ||
      std::abs(distance.at({0, 0}) - std::sqrt(5.)) > 1e-7)
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(mask.to(n::DType::Float32), {0}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(distance, {0}), -1, 3);
  a.title("Known3 by3 foreground")
      .x_label("column")
      .y_label("row")
      .x_limits(-.5, 6.5)
      .y_limits(-.5, 4.5);
  b.title("Signed distance[-1,3]")
      .x_label("column")
      .y_label("row")
      .x_limits(-.5, 6.5)
      .y_limits(-.5, 4.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1200, 560).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/segmentation_losses_distance.svg");
  std::print("Centre -1; foreground boundary0; corner sqrt(5)={:.9f}; outside horizontal "
             "distance2. Native100 rectangular exhaustive oracles pass.\n",
             distance.at({0, 0}));
}
```
